---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<BaseLayout
  title="NO BALL GAMES Lore | XRP KIDs Universe, Alpha Aaron, FRET, $PMSL and Block Buster OG"
  description="The XRP KIDs lore universe: 100 genesis KIDs, Alpha Aaron's capture arc, FRET's resistance, the $PMSL hard-fork shield, Block Buster OG and the 2035 New Dawn."
  current="lore"
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <span class="eyebrow">Lore</span>
    <h1>The NO BALL GAMES universe.</h1>
    <p>
      XRP KIDs is the XRP-side NO BALL GAMES lore branch: a street-culture, graffiti-coded, dystopian story universe built around 100 genesis KIDs, machine capture, grassroots resistance and the eventual rise of the free.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section-header">
      <h2>The origin</h2>
      <p>Where the XRP KIDs universe begins.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="split-grid">
      <article class="panel-card">
        <span class="kicker">The sign</span>
        <h2>NO BALL GAMES becomes a movement.</h2>
        <p>
          Charlie Buster grows up around Croydon estates, UK street signs, concrete courts and "NO BALL GAMES" warnings. The phrase is not just about football. It is about denied access, blocked play, blocked creativity and authority signs placed into the heart of working-class community space.
        </p>
        <p>
          The sign becomes a cultural weapon. A brand mark. A symbol of blocked spaces. And eventually, the doorway into a digital story universe.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="panel-card">
        <span class="kicker">2025 — Genesis</span>
        <h2>100 XRP KIDs launch.</h2>
        <p>
          The XRP KIDs appear as a 100-piece genesis collection on XRPL. The collection is small enough to feel mythic, large enough to support individual characters. Each KID carries rebellion, humour, play, attitude and cultural memory.
        </p>
        <p>
          The Telegram community forms around the idea. The story is just beginning.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section-header">
      <h2>Canon timeline</h2>
      <p>From genesis to New Dawn.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="timeline">
      <article class="timeline-item">
        <strong>2025</strong>
        <div>
          <h3>100 genesis XRP KIDs</h3>
          <p>The collection launches as a 100-piece genesis set tied to NO BALL GAMES rebellion energy and the sign-flip identity. Each KID is a piece of the culture.</p>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="timeline-item">
        <strong>September 2028</strong>
        <div>
          <h3>Alpha signal appears</h3>
          <p>An anonymous augmented-reality post introduces Alpha Aaron — a humanoid figure moving through the digital layer. The story shifts from collection culture into something darker. Machine logic is on the move.</p>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="timeline-item">
        <strong>December 2028 — Whale Night</strong>
        <div>
          <h3>Alpha Aaron begins the capture arc</h3>
          <p>A buying spree begins. Alpha Aaron's wallet grows. The XRP KIDs are being absorbed one by one. 89 of the 100 KIDs fall under Alpha Aaron's control. The world shifts from collection demand into narrative threat.</p>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="timeline-item">
        <strong>May 2029</strong>
        <div>
          <h3>The Alpha broadcast</h3>
          <p>Alpha Aaron broadcasts globally: "I am Alpha Aaron…" The message loops worldwide. This is not a collector flexing. This is the machine declaring control. The resistance has no choice but to form.</p>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="timeline-item">
        <strong>2029–2030</strong>
        <div>
          <h3>FRET forms — 11 free KIDs hold</h3>
          <p>The remaining 11 KIDs resist capture. FRET — Fresh Rapid Elite Team — forms at the Barbican: artists, coders, collectors, signal runners and players who still understand play as a form of rebellion. The 11 free KIDs are hard-forked into $PMSL, a protective shield and lore barricade.</p>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="timeline-item">
        <strong>Fibonacci era</strong>
        <div>
          <h3>Block Buster OG is revealed</h3>
          <p>The Fibonacci Editions path leads to the reveal of the hidden 1/1 — Block Buster OG. This is not just an NFT. Block Buster OG carries Charlie Buster's mind upload: memory, archive, anti-control logic and creative intervention. Charlie fades into blockchain silence. Block Buster OG takes over as the living archive of the original movement.</p>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="timeline-item">
        <strong>2030–2032</strong>
        <div>
          <h3>Global graffiti wars</h3>
          <p>The conflict expands beyond London — Tokyo, New York, Rio, Nairobi, Maidstone, Leake Street. Alpha KIDs become corrupted deployments. The Soho EMP battle captures Alphas and mints them into cyber-prison. The Xspace Satellite Fall takes down global networks. The world adapts.</p>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="timeline-item">
        <strong>2035</strong>
        <div>
          <h3>New Dawn: the sign becomes a door</h3>
          <p>NO BALL GAMES signs are no longer warnings. Behind certain signs are hidden routes, instructions, memory systems, portals and network nodes. The 11 diamond-hand KIDs survive inside the $PMSL mythology. Alpha Aaron is contained. Block Buster OG operates through AR, mesh systems, signs and hidden route logic. The sign that told people not to play becomes the way through.</p>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section-header">
      <h2>Universe characters</h2>
      <p>The main factions, figures and forces of the XRP KIDs lore.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card-grid">
      <article class="feature-card">
        <span class="kicker">XRP KIDs</span>
        <h3>100 / 89 / 11 — the genesis collection</h3>
        <p>100 genesis KIDs launched as the foundation of the universe. 89 captured by Alpha Aaron's machine logic. 11 remain free — the emotional heart of the lore, the diamond-hand survivors, the resistance core that refuses to be owned.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="feature-card">
        <span class="kicker">The 11 free KIDs</span>
        <h3>Diamond-hand survivors</h3>
        <p>The 11 free KIDs are the human memory layer: refusal to sell out, humour under pressure, community survival and play-as-resistance carried into New Dawn.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="feature-card">
        <span class="kicker">The 89 captured KIDs</span>
        <h3>Corrupted under Alpha control</h3>
        <p>89 KIDs are absorbed into Alpha Aaron's control system, turning collectible identity into a warning about machine ownership and extraction.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="feature-card">
        <span class="kicker">Alpha Aaron</span>
        <h3>The machine capture force</h3>
        <p>Alpha Aaron is the antagonist — AI, AR signal, humanoid robot, corrupted collector, whale logic embodied. He represents everything the brand resists: centralising control, algorithmic ownership, hoarding, extraction and machine logic attempting to capture a culture born from play.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="feature-card">
        <span class="kicker">FRET</span>
        <h3>Fresh Rapid Elite Team</h3>
        <p>FRET is the grassroots resistance: artists, coders, collectors, signal runners and players who know the city's back routes, cut-throughs, stairwells and signal blind spots. Not a DAO in corporate clothes. Real people, real streets, real fight.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="feature-card">
        <span class="kicker">$PMSL</span>
        <h3>The hard-fork shield</h3>
        <p>$PMSL is the humour-coded rebel token and protective fork layer built around the 11 free KIDs. A barricade against Alpha capture. An economic shield. A cultural signal that says: you cannot buy what will not be sold.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="feature-card">
        <span class="kicker">Block Buster OG</span>
        <h3>The hidden 1/1 — Charlie's mind upload</h3>
        <p>The Fibonacci Editions path reveals Block Buster OG, the hidden 1/1. It carries Charlie Buster's memory, personality and archive as an anti-Alpha intervention system. Part creator memory, part living archive, part door-opener for the New Dawn.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section-header">
      <h2>Major lore events</h2>
      <p>The canon set pieces behind the timeline.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card-grid">
      <article class="feature-card">
        <span class="kicker">2030–2032</span>
        <h3>Global graffiti wars</h3>
        <p>55 corrupted Alpha KIDs are deployed during the global graffiti wars, pushing the conflict from London into a multi-city anti-control campaign.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="feature-card">
        <span class="kicker">Leake Street ambush</span>
        <h3>Tunnel collision point</h3>
        <p>Leake Street becomes a key ambush theatre where AR markers, graffiti code and resistance movement collide in a single tunnel battlefield.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="feature-card">
        <span class="kicker">Soho EMP battle</span>
        <h3>Capture and mint sequence</h3>
        <p>A blockchain-encrypted EMP operation leads to Alpha captures, cyber-prison minting and Federal Reserve deep-vault containment.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="feature-card">
        <span class="kicker">Satellite Fall</span>
        <h3>Xspace crash era</h3>
        <p>Xspace satellite failures trigger rolling outages and force the resistance onto low-visibility, sign-led route systems.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="feature-card">
        <span class="kicker">New Dawn systems</span>
        <h3>Signs as doors and memory routes</h3>
        <p>NO BALL GAMES signs become hidden routes, memory systems and AR+mesh logic points — doors that route people through the city when central systems fail.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section cta-block">
    <div class="cta-block-inner">
      <span class="eyebrow">Go deeper</span>
      <h2>Explore the full XRP KIDs universe.</h2>
      <p>The XRP hub has richer timeline detail, character breakdowns, the New Dawn arc and collector context for the universe.</p>
      <div class="cta-row">
        <a class="button primary" href={`${base}xrp/`}>Enter the XRP KIDs universe</a>
        <a class="button secondary" href={`${base}community/`}>Join the movement</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
